      "footnotes": [
        "(B) This was a joint loan by the Kincheng Banking Corporation and the Salt Industry Bank.",
        "(15) The term of these loans was for six months.",
        "(C) This loan was made by the \"Company of the Four Provinces along the Tientsin-Pukow Line.\"",
        "(16) Two loans amounting to $800,000 were concluded in February 1921. Later $100,000 were repaid. In December 1921 the total amount of interest and capital together with advance of $200,000 all due for repayment was little over $1,002,000. Arrangement was subsequently made to repay to the extent of little over $202,000 with the Salt Surplus, leaving $800,000 outstanding.",
        "(17) A certain portion of the loan has been repaid from time to time, leaving the outstanding amount unpaid. As to the method of repayment, there is no definite arrangement.",
        "(18) The term of the loan was for one month only. The repayment has been deferred once and again.",
        "(19) The term was for three months. The repayment has been much deferred.",
        "(20) The term was fixed to be six months. Deducting the amount already returned, the outstanding amount is overdue for payment.",
        "(21) The term was for four months. It was however rearranged that the whole amount would be redeemed in sixteen monthly instalments commencing in October 1922 with Salt Surplus.",
        "(22) Altogether the term was fixed to be four months, no repayment has ever been made till now.",
        "(23) It was understood that the loan would be fully returned in six months' time with the revenue of the stamp tax. However, deducting the amount already paid, the outstanding amount has to be redeemed.",
        "(24) The term was for three years. No repayment has ever been made.",
        "(D) This was a joint loan by the Hua Fu Bank, Chung Yuan Bank and the Yung Ta Bank.",
        "(25) The term was for two months. Nothing has been repaid till now.",
        "(26) The term was for six months. Nothing has been repaid till now.",
        "(27) It was originally agreed to have the loan repaid in two instalments in December 1919 and June 1921. Although a portion was redeemed, the outstanding amount has been due for payment.",
        "(E) These are the cost of purchases and supplies for the Kung Hsien Arsenal, in Honan.",
        "(28) The original understanding was to repay $10,000 every month with the profit of the Wuchang Government Mint commencing in January 1922.",
        "(29) The loan was originally made for a period of 24 months and was secured on the revenues of the three customs, namely, Wuchang, Hsinti and Ichang. No returns have been received from Hupeh as to how much of the loan has been repaid with the said revenue."
      ],
      "context": "The page gives the grand totals of outstanding short-term internal debts in dollar equivalents by currency, followed by explanatory notes on the individual loans.",
